{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>A land flowing with milk and honey.</b> This section concludes thus, and adjoins to it שמע ישראל, to explain that the ultimate intent of inheriting it with all this pleasure is only so that we may inherit what is intended for it — and that is the ד׳ of אחד, which is the Will that bestows mercy and judgment; and this is the sense of 'a land flowing with milk and honey.' So too he mentioned this in the verse (Deuteronomy 8:8): ״ארץ חטה ושעורה״, and he brought proof for intellectual pleasure from honey, which is bodily pleasure — and understand this."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:45:57.100833635Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}